Dear Cyranor

Happy to. Before Erra cuts anything I would be cautious about four things, an=
d I would rather raise them now than in the Council Chamber.

1. Which gap. I assume the Elf to Dwarf good honours gap, as in the annual re=
port. If Council means something else (progression, continuation, grades), sa=
y so, because the answers differ.

2. Which year. The most recent graduates we can report on are 1052 (completed=
 1051-52). The 1053 graduates will not exist until the summer boards. So "the=
 latest figure" for a May paper is the one Council already saw in November: 2=
1.5 percentage points. If the paper quotes anything else as current, it is wr=
ong.

3. By programme. The denominator here is the problem. Each programme graduate=
s somewhere between fifty and a hundred and thirty students a year; split by =
species, a few cells fall below twenty and we suppress them. A "by programme"=
 table will have gaps in it, and the programmes with the smallest cohorts wil=
l swing by ten points from one year to the next for no reason at all. I would=
 rather Council understood why than wondered what we were hiding, and I would=
 rather the Faculty did not set programme targets on single-year figures.

4. What Council actually asked for. Aerion's note, as I understand it, was fo=
r two pages: figures, what the Faculty will do, how you will know. The figure=
s part is a paragraph and a five-year table. We can supply that in a day. The=
 other two parts are yours, and I would gently suggest they are the harder bi=
t.

Erra's extract from October is half done; she was pulled onto the NSS work. S=
he can finish it by the 20th if that suits.

Subject to the caveats above, of course.

Quorin
